-- title:
--   Corollary 7: ORTHODIR directions are combinations of multiple scattering iterations
-- statement:
--   Let $V$ be a complex Hilbert space, $\mathcal T:V\to V$ a bounded linear operator, $g\in V$, $\eta^i=\mathcal T^ig$, and let $p^{(j)}$, $\beta_{ij}$ be generated by ORTHODIR for $\mathcal A=\mathcal I-\mathcal T$ with $p^{(0)}=g$. Then there are coefficients $\gamma_{ij}\in\mathbb C$ such that each $p^{(j)}$ is a linear combination of $\eta^0,\dots,\eta^j$,
--
--   $$p^{(j)}=\sum_{i=0}^{j}\gamma_{ij}\,\eta^i\qquad(j\ge0),$$
--
--   and the next direction is computed from them as
--
--   $$p^{(j+1)}=\sum_{i=0}^{j}\gamma_{ij}\,\eta^{i}-\sum_{i=0}^{j}\gamma_{ij}\,\eta^{i+1}+\sum_{i=0}^{j}\beta_{ij}\,p^{(i)}=\sum_{i=0}^{j+1}\gamma_{i,j+1}\,\eta^i.$$
--
--   This is the identification procedure that computes the ORTHODIR directions from the multiple scattering iterations, whose phases are known.
--
--   **Formalization Note** One family $\gamma_{ij}$ serves all $j$, so the last equality is the first identity at $j+1$. The paper gives no formula for $\gamma_{i,j+1}$ ("easily computed by identification"); the statement asserts existence. $\mathcal T$ is an arbitrary bounded operator, of which the paper's operator (7) is an instance.
-- source:
--   Boubendir, Ecevit and Reitich, Acceleration of an iterative method for the evaluation of high-frequency multiple scattering effects, arXiv:1606.00062v1 (2016), claim c008; Section 5, Corollary 7, eqs. (34)-(35), PDF p. 12

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_Arxiv1606_00062_Basic

open Filter Topology

namespace Arxiv1606_00062

theorem orthodir_identification {V : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup V] [InnerProductSpace ℂ V]
    [CompleteSpace V] (T : V →L[ℂ] V) (g : V) :
    ∃ γ : ℕ → ℕ → ℂ,
      (∀ j : ℕ, orthodirDir (1 - T) g j =
        ∑ i ∈ Finset.range (j + 1), γ i j • msIter T g i) ∧
      (∀ j : ℕ, orthodirDir (1 - T) g (j + 1) =
        ∑ i ∈ Finset.range (j + 1), γ i j • msIter T g i -
          ∑ i ∈ Finset.range (j + 1), γ i j • msIter T g (i + 1) +
          ∑ i ∈ Finset.range (j + 1), orthodirBeta (1 - T) g i j • orthodirDir (1 - T) g i) := by sorry

end Arxiv1606_00062
